<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>

  <!-- ===== Pipeline foundation (always run) ===== -->

  <!-- EN: base cost from tech level -->
  <UWU_BaseCostFromTechLevel.label>基于科技等级的基础成本</UWU_BaseCostFromTechLevel.label>
  <!-- EN: Provides a fallback base cost derived from the weapon's tech level. Ensures all weapons have a customization cost even if they lack a craftable recipe. Neolithic uses wood, medieval uses steel, industrial uses steel and components, and spacer and above use plasteel and advanced components -->
  <UWU_BaseCostFromTechLevel.description>提供一个由武器科技等级推算的备用基础成本。即使武器没有可制作的配方，也能确保它拥有自定义成本。石器时代使用原木，中世纪使用钢铁，工业时代使用钢铁与零部件，太空时代及以上使用玻璃钢与高级零部件。</UWU_BaseCostFromTechLevel.description>

  <!-- EN: base cost from recipe -->
  <UWU_BaseCostFromRecipe.label>基于配方的基础成本</UWU_BaseCostFromRecipe.label>
  <!-- EN: Replaces the tech-level fallback with the weapon's actual crafting recipe costs, including both fixed ingredients and stuff costs. Only acts when the weapon has a craftable base definition. -->
  <UWU_BaseCostFromRecipe.description>用武器实际的制作配方成本取代按科技等级推算的备用成本，其中同时包含固定原料与材料成本。仅在武器拥有可制作的基础定义时才会生效。</UWU_BaseCostFromRecipe.description>

  <!-- EN: quality multiplier -->
  <UWU_QualityMultiplier.label>品质倍率</UWU_QualityMultiplier.label>
  <!-- EN: Scales costs based on weapon quality. Higher-quality weapons cost more to customize. Includes the base 50% cost fraction so each trait costs half the weapon's full recipe value before quality scaling. -->
  <UWU_QualityMultiplier.description>根据武器品质缩放成本。品质越高的武器，自定义成本越高。其中已包含50%的基础成本比例，因此在品质缩放之前，每项特性的成本为武器完整配方价值的一半。</UWU_QualityMultiplier.description>

  <!-- EN: rarity multiplier -->
  <UWU_RarityMultiplier.label>稀有度倍率</UWU_RarityMultiplier.label>
  <!-- EN: Scales costs by how rare the trait is. A trait that appears half as often as a common one costs twice as much to fit, and the increase is capped there. Negative traits are not scaled. -->
  <UWU_RarityMultiplier.description>根据特性的稀有程度缩放成本。出现频率只有常见特性一半的特性，自定义成本会翻倍，且涨幅到此封顶。负面特性不进行此项缩放。</UWU_RarityMultiplier.description>

  <!-- EN: negative trait material downgrade -->
  <UWU_NegativeDowngrade.label>负面特性材料降级</UWU_NegativeDowngrade.label>
  <!-- EN: Downgrades cost materials by one technology level for negative traits. Spacer components become industrial, plasteel becomes steel, steel becomes wood. Reflects that negative modifications use cruder, cheaper techniques. -->
  <UWU_NegativeDowngrade.description>将负面特性的成本材料降低一个科技等级。高级零部件变为零部件，玻璃钢变为钢铁，钢铁变为原木。这体现出负面改造所用的手法更为粗糙、廉价。</UWU_NegativeDowngrade.description>

  <!-- ===== Thematic rules (keyword-matched) ===== -->

  <!-- labelKeywords, whole-list injections: every English keyword is kept
       verbatim (those are what match the language-invariant defName tokens) and
       confirmed zh-Hans trait labels are appended. A zh-Hans label carries no
       ASCII space or hyphen, so it is a single token and a keyword can only
       match a trait whose ENTIRE label equals it; every token below is an exact
       label shipped by Unique Melee Weapons or vanilla Odyssey.
       Deliberately omitted: 握把 and 镶嵌 (bare roots that match nothing -
       CustomGrip's label is 定制握把 and the inlays are 黄金镶嵌 / 翡翠镶嵌),
       宙斯 / 单分子剑 / 等离子剑 (weapon-name roots, no trait uses them alone),
       舒适 (extrapolated from the Comfort StatDef, no confirmed trait wording),
       and 重型弹 for UWU_Oversized (vanilla's OversizedRounds is ammo framing,
       not an oversized weapon). 头重 and 配重 ARE shipped despite being short,
       generic engineering words, per the scouting judgment that a misapplied
       stuff swap is low-stakes. UWU_HeavyScrap gets no injection at all: it
       sets requireAllKeywords, so appending anything would demand all entries
       at once and break the English heavy+scrap pair, and zh-Hans could never
       supply two space-delimited tokens anyway. -->

  <!-- EN: toxic component swap -->
  <UWU_ToxSwap.label>剧毒零部件替换</UWU_ToxSwap.label>
  <!-- EN: Replaces components with herbal medicine (3x the component count), reflecting the organic toxins needed. Weapons whose costs carry no components instead add herbal medicine scaled to the weapon's crafting complexity. -->
  <UWU_ToxSwap.description>将零部件替换为草药（数量为零部件的3倍），以体现所需的有机毒素。若武器的成本中不含零部件，则改为按武器的制作复杂度追加相应数量的草药。</UWU_ToxSwap.description>
  <!-- EN: tox, toxic, paralytic, acid-injector, venom, envenomed, poisoned, opiated, sedative -->
  <UWU_ToxSwap.labelKeywords>
    <li>tox</li>
    <li>toxic</li>
    <li>paralytic</li>
    <li>acid-injector</li>
    <li>venom</li>
    <li>envenomed</li>
    <li>poisoned</li>
    <li>opiated</li>
    <li>sedative</li>
    <li>淬毒</li>
    <li>阿片涂层</li>
    <li>剧毒弹</li>
  </UWU_ToxSwap.labelKeywords>

  <!-- EN: incendiary component swap -->
  <UWU_IncendiarySwap.label>燃烧零部件替换</UWU_IncendiarySwap.label>
  <!-- EN: Replaces components with chemfuel (10x the component count), reflecting the volatile fuel needed. Advanced components count as components here. Weapons whose costs carry no components instead add chemfuel scaled to the weapon's crafting complexity. -->
  <UWU_IncendiarySwap.description>将零部件替换为化合燃料（数量为零部件的10倍），以体现所需的易挥发燃料。此处高级零部件同样算作零部件。若武器的成本中不含零部件，则改为按武器的制作复杂度追加相应数量的化合燃料。</UWU_IncendiarySwap.description>
  <!-- EN: incendiary, blast, blasts, pitch-soaked, detonation, chemburster, flaming, searing, burning, ember -->
  <UWU_IncendiarySwap.labelKeywords>
    <li>incendiary</li>
    <li>blast</li>
    <li>blasts</li>
    <li>pitch-soaked</li>
    <li>detonation</li>
    <li>chemburster</li>
